:CATCH and :FINALLY left in a procedure after their :TRY and :ENDTRY were
deleted. Both are stray_block_keyword; catch_order_before_finally and
single_catch must not claim them (diag.stray_block_keyword first Flags
fence). The :CATCH form is correct, so catch_clause_form is silent.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE StoreResult;
	:PARAMETERS nValue;
	:DECLARE nStored;
	nStored := nValue;
	:CATCH;
	nStored := 0;
	:FINALLY;
	nStored := nStored + 0;
	:RETURN nStored;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE StoreResult;
	:PARAMETERS nValue;
	:DECLARE nStored;
	nStored := nValue;
:CATCH;
	nStored := 0;
:FINALLY;
	nStored := nStored + 0;
	:RETURN nStored;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
5:2-5:8 error stray_block_keyword: ':CATCH' is outside any ':TRY' block
7:2-7:10 error stray_block_keyword: ':FINALLY' is outside any ':TRY' block
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
5:2-5:8 error stray_block_keyword: ':CATCH' is outside any ':TRY' block
7:2-7:10 error stray_block_keyword: ':FINALLY' is outside any ':TRY' block
